# Direct runtime dependencies of the `crisistwin_agent` package.
# Everything this package needs beyond the Anthropic SDK is in the Python
# standard library; the Rothermel physics stays in TypeScript and is reached
# through the Node sidecar, not through a Python science stack.
#
# The agent loop uses `client.beta.messages.tool_runner` and the `@beta_tool`
# decorator. Those live in the SDK's beta namespace and can change shape within
# a major version, so the range is held to the major the agent was written
# against and the resolved set in requirements.txt is what gets installed.
anthropic>=2.3.0,<3
